Description: Multi-protocol honeypot fingerprinter CLI
 honeypot-auditor fingerprints whether an authorized target behaves like a
 low-interaction honeypot. It probes banners and protocol state across common
 services (SSH, HTTP, Redis, MQTT, SNMP, Elasticsearch, and others) and
 produces a weighted score without sending exploits.
 .
 Public targets require an explicit --confirm-authorized flag. Probe only
 systems you own or have permission to test.
 .
 Optional features (nmap version scans, Redis client helpers, SOCKS, Scapy)
 are available via Recommends/Suggests or pip install "honeypot-auditor[full]".
